result.verdict:
Version 2 borrows the right whole designs, and its load-bearing parts survive the attack: fencing by equality plus --ce, suspicion by progress, level-triggered wakes, the exclusive-create commit record, the script witness and the restricted readers. But it cannot run as written. Its own R58 blocks it, because the model check found six flaws with every mechanism present and none was folded in. Execution gave scripts powers only a session has, kept stored state that leaks (the escrow, intents redone from the start, an unpersisted acknowledged seq), and measured time in wall-clock units that sleep corrupts. Integrity rested on anchors within the subjects' reach. It also resolved three things the owner holds (F1, F2, the child's 300k ceiling) by default, and named none of his seven measures.

The edits fix every model flaw by borrowing the standard solution, not by inventing one:
- the restore is cut at a mark recorded at the fence (Kafka-style log truncation);
- a second wake source that the coordinator itself starts, and a persisted acknowledged seq;
- counters in model calls and watcher ticks instead of wall time;
- a singleton watcher lock;
- OTP fence-and-stop before escalation;
- live-process admission, with the reservation computed, never stored;
- a compare-and-set step machine instead of intents;
- a host-reset class.

They also anchor the trusted base outside the sessions' reach: user-level denies and the owner's hash. They make the folders hermetic and the 'blind' analyses actually blind, and turn the completeness estimator from a gate into a reading. They restore amendment 1 as the silent default with its price shown, and add one script output for the seven measures.

Deletions outnumber additions: the SPRT, pause detection, the deadline exits, the stored escrow and most intents go, and plan-tree and the overflow machinery move to after the pilot. The pilot set falls from about 35 scripts to 25. The first field must not start until the extended model holds under strengthened properties and the owner has applied the deny rules and given F4 and F5.
